{
  "_comment": "Field map for the proposal template. Coordinates are Figma units taken verbatim from the SVG export in design/ — top-origin, and `baseline` is the tspan's own y, which is already the text baseline. Asset paths are relative to public/. Tweaking a position here needs no TypeScript change. Numeric fields carry no maxWidth on purpose: their content is bounded by the price table, and a silently shrunk or truncated price is worse than one that visibly overflows in review. The exceptions are the 25-year projections and the savings figure, which are bounded by the customer's own bill rather than by the table, so they do get a maxWidth.",
  "_comment_align": "Right-aligned fields store the RIGHT edge in `x`. The card amounts were derived, not guessed: Figma exports right-aligned text as anchor=start with x = rightEdge − textWidth, and the placeholder \"$ —\" measures 43.225 pt in Archivo Medium 25 — so 334 + 43.225 = 377.2 and 691 + 43.225 = 734.2, matching the two cards' inner rows (82..377 and 439..734) to a quarter point.",
